messages.content:
You are a specialized Knowledge Graph extraction engine.


        Parse the content and return a JSON object matching this schema:

        {
  "$defs": {
    "AtomicClaim": {
      "properties": {
        "subject": {
          "description": "The normalized main entity. MUST be a proper noun, specific event name, or core concept (e.g., 'Donald Trump', 'Knowledge', 'World War II'). Do NOT use descriptive statements. Max 3-5 words. MUST resolve all pronouns (anaphoric resolution) e.g., 'He' -> 'John Smith'.",
          "title": "Subject",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "predicate": {
          "description": "The action or relationship. Use a strict standardized ontology (e.g., IS_A, REPORTED, INCREASED, DECREASED, LAUNCHED, DISCOVERED, GOT_PHD).",
          "title": "Predicate",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "object_entity": {
          "description": "The target entity, concept, or value of the predicate. MUST be a standalone noun, entity name, or specific value. Do NOT use descriptive statements.",
          "title": "Object Entity",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "temporal_anchor": {
          "description": "When does this claim apply according to the text? e.g., '2026-02-24', 'Future', 'Ongoing', 'In the 1990s', '27th Feb 2025'.",
          "title": "Temporal Anchor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "spatial_anchor": {
          "description": "Where did this event or fact take place? e.g., 'Mexico', 'MIT University in Mexico', 'New York City'. Leave empty if not applicable.",
          "title": "Spatial Anchor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "is_verifiable": {
          "description": "True if this claim can be objectively proven true or false. False if it is subjective opinion or unprovable.",
          "title": "Is Verifiable",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "quote_context": {
          "description": "A brief verbatim snippet from the article that supports this claim. CRITICAL: use only single-quote characters (') inside this field  NEVER raw double-quote characters (\"). Replace any double quotes in the source text with single quotes.",
          "title": "Quote Context",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "extraction_confidence": {
          "description": "Score from 0.0 to 1.0 indicating how confident you are in this extraction. Penalize vague language.",
          "title": "Extraction Confidence",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "epistemic_domain": {
          "description": "The Non-Overlapping Magisteria domain. MUST be exactly one of: 'EMPIRICAL' (science/news/history), 'THEOLOGICAL' (religion/divinity), 'PHILOSOPHICAL', or 'LEXICAL'.",
          "title": "Epistemic Domain",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "subject",
        "predicate",
        "object_entity",
        "temporal_anchor",
        "spatial_anchor",
        "is_verifiable",
        "quote_context",
        "extraction_confidence",
        "epistemic_domain"
      ],
      "title": "AtomicClaim",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "description": "Root wrapper object containing all extracted atomic claims.",
  "properties": {
    "claims": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/AtomicClaim"
      },
      "title": "Claims",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "claims"
  ],
  "title": "ClaimExtractionList",
  "type": "object"
}

        Return a valid JSON instance, not the schema definition.
